  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\nIssued at 141 PM CDT MON JUL 20 2026\n\nMost computer models, and the official NHC forecast, has what is\ncurrently TD2 moving generally westward over the next couple of\ndays. This track will keep the system from having any direct\nsignificant impacts on our weather here in central Alabama.\n\nSort of indirectly, it looks like we will be in a bit of an area\nof subsidence just beyond the periphery of the tropical system.\nThis should help to keep afternoon convection to a relative\nminimum through the day tomorrow, with the possible exception of\nthe far southeastern counties. This will also help keep\ntemperatures a bit higher than normal as well. Highest heat index\nvalues will be close to advisory criteria on Tuesday, and will\ncontinue the Heat Advisory as is.\n\nWe start to get into more of a northwest flow upper air pattern by\nthe end of the week, as the big upper high becomes more\nestablished out west and a trough starts to dig into the east.\nThis should get temperatures back down to more manageable levels,\nwhile also opening the door of opportunity for thunderstorm\nclusters/MCSs to affect our area. \n\n/61/",
